    {
      "additions": 2,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/blob/4342f1f5c68924d66c97ac7bbf47138e6e4e6c70/torchtitan%2Fmodels%2Fdeepseek_v3%2FMTP.md",
      "changes": 3,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/torchtitan/contents/torchtitan%2Fmodels%2Fdeepseek_v3%2FMTP.md?ref=4342f1f5c68924d66c97ac7bbf47138e6e4e6c70",
      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "torchtitan/models/deepseek_v3/MTP.md",
      "patch": "@@ -250,7 +250,8 @@ total_loss = main_loss + mtp_scale * mean(mtp_losses)\n \n Preprocessing also produces separate target-token and routed-token count\n vectors ordered as `(main, depth 1, ..., depth N)`. The trainer sums both\n-vectors over the optimizer step and reduces them together. Each prediction\n+vectors over the optimizer step. Routing counts reduce on every MoE stage;\n+loss counts reduce only on loss-owning pipeline stages. Each prediction\n loss uses its target count, while each MoE auxiliary loss uses the routed-token\n count for the block that owns it. This keeps instruction-style label masking\n independent from MoE routing.",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/raw/4342f1f5c68924d66c97ac7bbf47138e6e4e6c70/torchtitan%2Fmodels%2Fdeepseek_v3%2FMTP.md",
